 "structural_change": "STW-S81c-HEAD-TILE 10-22 successor of r6km (FAIL 03:15) on the same R6 RTL 22a89b512 and geometry (648 = H10 reserve), regional k-means clock roots kept. Measured cause of ALL four R6-RTL gates (r6m/r6f/r6km/r6kf): 3_3_place_gp timing-driven repair RSZ-3006 (ODB-1211: native fp32 adder cells are dont_touch, GPL stretched a native net and could not buffer before its dont_touch load), so CTS never ran and the >15k/root clock_domain item had no measured spread (FAIL). Fix: physical/common_flow/native_dt_release.tcl (PRE_GLOBAL_PLACE) clears the ODB dont_touch on *u_native.* cells (all 451k native dont_touch cells; tested on the r6km 3_2 odb: 451,629 -> 0) after the mapped native census, so the resizer may buffer/resize them (Boolean graph and census-proven loads unchanged, loads only drop). R5f synth: ~126k flops on ONE TritonCTS root over 648 um (gate WARN clock_span; 8x the 15k/root guidance; no head tile ever reached CTS). Here the ck port net is split by placed-sink 2-D k-means into 16 regional clock roots (physical/common_flow/clock_split_km.tcl, closed precedent dscoll_lane_w_s12h K32 at 725.8 x 583.2): one BUFx24 local root per region (~7875 sinks, ~162 um span), CTS builds one short tree per region under a balanced top tree; leaf groups 16 sinks / 24 um. Same port, clock, flops, constraints, cycles and pins; one external clock root (die binding unchanged). Pin flops at faces (io_flop_at_pins) join their face regions.",
 "reset_landing": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "Top RTL explicitly implements three synchronous face landing stages in kept source families2/64/1536 with standard equivalence-proven redistribution; an additional kit wrapper would double land reset. Startup assertion/release +1 edge versus old two-stage kit is recorded, traffic unchanged."
 },
